Posted as "[freebsd-ports PATCH] mail/notmuch-git: Synchronize Notmuch
tags through a git repository" [1].

It is a new slave port, not the change to mail/notmuch I sketched
earlier. The script needs Python and git at run time, and mail/notmuch
has neither, so installing it from the master port would add both to
every notmuch user's dependencies. The tree already splits notmuch's
extras this way, with mail/notmuch-mutt as the script-only example,
and Debian ships notmuch-git as a package of its own. The
notmuch-git(1) man page stays in mail/notmuch, which installs it
already.

I was also wrong that there is no ports tree here. The freebsd-port
skill keeps one in /var/tmp/freebsd-ports. The port's only build
dependency is pkg, so I staged and packaged it without building
anything else. stage, check-plist and package pass, and the staged
notmuch-git runs. The package depends on git, notmuch and python312.
portlint has one warning, about PORTREVISION=0 in a new port; the
patch notes explain why that line stays. I have not run it under
poudriere testport.

